{"mode":"training","language":"en","altTextLanguage":"","title":"","instruction":{"english":"","german":""},"allowInstructionLineBreaks":false,"readingText":{"instruction":{"german":"","english":""},"content":"","configs":[]},"sequences":[{"instruction":{"german":"<p>Read the rules in the grammar box. <\/p>","english":""},"configs":[],"staticConfigs":[],"parts":["<p><b>Grammar | <em>should<\/em><\/b><\/p><p>\u2022 We use <em>should<\/em> + verb to give advice.<\/p><p><em>You <\/em><b><em>should <\/em><\/b><em>eat more fruit.<\/em><\/p><p>\u2022 The negative is <em>shouldn\u2019t<\/em>. To make questions, we put <em>should <\/em>in front of the subject.<\/p><p><em>You <\/em><b><em>shouldn\u2019t <\/em><\/b><em>do this.<\/em><\/p><p><b><em>Should we<\/em><\/b><em> arrive early?<\/em><\/p><p>\u2022 We can also use <em>should <\/em>with an if-clause to give advice.<\/p><p><em>If you want to feel good, you <\/em><b><em>should <\/em><\/b><em>do more exercise.<\/em><\/p>"],"globalTypesConfigs":[{"type":"gap","widthMode":"adaptToContent","longestAlternativeSolutions":false,"ignoreCaseSensitivity":false}],"staticText":{"text":"<p><br><\/p>","backgroundColor":"lightgray","isSet":false}},{"instruction":{"english":"","german":"<p>Make new sentences with the information and words in brackets.<\/p>"},"parts":["<p><b>1<\/b> You should eat chocolate. (he \/ not)<\/p><p><em style=\"color: rgb(0, 102, 204);\">He shouldn\u2019t eat chocolate.<\/em><\/p><p><b>2<\/b> You shouldn\u2019t talk loudly. (they)<\/p><p><gap id=\"gap_0\"><\/gap><\/p><p><b>3<\/b> I should listen to you. (?)<\/p><p><gap id=\"gap_1\"><\/gap><\/p><p><b>4<\/b> He should do something. (we \/ ?)<\/p><p><gap id=\"gap_2\"><\/gap><\/p><p><b>5<\/b> They should ask the teacher. (you \/ not)<\/p><p><gap id=\"gap_3\"><\/gap><\/p><p><b>6<\/b> We shouldn\u2019t take the bus. (+ \/ the train)<\/p><p><gap id=\"gap_4\"><\/gap><\/p>"],"configs":[{"correctAnswer":"They shouldn\u2019t talk loudly.","additionalAnswers":[],"id":"gap_0